  (134, 'Vaporeon', 1, 'water', null, 'Bubble Jet Pokémon', 10, 290, 'When Vaporeon’s fins begin to vibrate, it is a sign that rain will come within a few hours.', 133, 'Water Stone'),
  (135, 'Jolteon', 1, 'electric', null, 'Lightning Pokémon', 8, 245, 'It concentrates the weak electric charges emitted by its cells and launches wicked lightning bolts.', 133, 'Thunder Stone'),
  (136, 'Flareon', 1, 'fire', null, 'Flame Pokémon', 9, 250, 'It stores some of the air it inhales in its internal flame pouch, which heats it to over 3,000 degrees Fahrenheit.', 133, 'Fire Stone'),
  (137, 'Porygon', 1, 'normal', null, 'Virtual Pokémon', 8, 365, 'It is a manmade Pokémon. Since it doesn’t breathe, people are eager to try it in any environment.', null, null),
  (138, 'Omanyte', 1, 'rock', 'water', 'Spiral Pokémon', 4, 75, 'Revived from an ancient fossil, this Pokémon uses air stored in its shell to sink and rise in water.', null, null),
  (139, 'Omastar', 1, 'rock', 'water', 'Spiral Pokémon', 10, 350, 'Apparently, it cracked Shellder’s shell with its sharp fangs and sucked out the insides.', 138, 'Level 40'),
  (140, 'Kabuto', 1, 'rock', 'water', 'Shellfish Pokémon', 5, 115, 'On rare occasions, some have been found as fossils which they became while hiding on the ocean floor.', null, null),
  (141, 'Kabutops', 1, 'rock', 'water', 'Shellfish Pokémon', 13, 405, 'In the water, it tucks in its limbs to become more compact, then it wiggles its shell to swim fast.', 140, 'Level 40'),
  (142, 'Aerodactyl', 1, 'rock', 'flying', 'Fossil Pokémon', 18, 590, 'A vicious Pokémon from the distant past, it appears to have flown by spreading its wings and gliding.', null, null),
  (143, 'Snorlax', 1, 'normal', null, 'Sleeping Pokémon', 21, 4600, 'What sounds like its cry may actually be its snores or the rumblings of its hungry belly.', null, null),
  (144, 'Articuno', 1, 'ice', 'flying', 'Freeze Pokémon', 17, 554, 'The magnificent, seemingly translucent wings of this legendary bird Pokémon are said to be made of ice.', null, null),
  (145, 'Zapdos', 1, 'electric', 'flying', 'Electric Pokémon', 16, 526, 'This legendary bird Pokémon causes savage thunderstorms by flapping its glittering wings.', null, null),
  (146, 'Moltres', 1, 'fire', 'flying', 'Flame Pokémon', 20, 600, 'This legendary Pokémon scatters embers with every flap of its wings. It is a thrilling sight to behold.', null, null),
  (147, 'Dratini', 1, 'dragon', null, 'Dragon Pokémon', 18, 33, 'It is born large to start with. It repeatedly sheds its skin as it steadily grows longer.', null, null),
  (148, 'Dragonair', 1, 'dragon', null, 'Dragon Pokémon', 40, 165, 'They say that if it emits an aura from its whole body, the weather will begin to change instantly.', 147, 'Level 30'),
  (149, 'Dragonite', 1, 'dragon', 'flying', 'Dragon Pokémon', 22, 2100, 'It is said that this Pokémon constantly flies over the immense seas and rescues drowning people.', 148, 'Level 55'),
  (150, 'Mewtwo', 1, 'psychic', null, 'Genetic Pokémon', 20, 1220, 'Because its battle abilities were raised to the ultimate level, it thinks only of defeating its foes.', null, null),
  (151, 'Mew', 1, 'psychic', null, 'New Species Pokémon', 4, 40, 'Apparently, it appears only to those people who are pure of heart and have a strong desire to see it.', null, null),
  (152, 'Chikorita', 2, 'grass', null, 'Leaf Pokémon', 9, 64, 'A sweet aroma gently wafts from the leaf on its head. It is docile and loves to soak up sunrays.', null, null),
  (153, 'Bayleef', 2, 'grass', null, 'Leaf Pokémon', 12, 158, 'The scent of spices comes from around its neck. Somehow, sniffing it makes you want to fight.', 152, 'Level 16'),
  (154, 'Meganium', 2, 'grass', null, 'Herb Pokémon', 18, 1005, 'The aroma that rises from its petals contains a substance that calms aggressive feelings.', 153, 'Level 32'),
  (155, 'Cyndaquil', 2, 'fire', null, 'Fire Mouse Pokémon', 5, 79, 'It is timid, and always curls itself up in a ball. If attacked, it flares up its back for protection.', null, null),
  (156, 'Quilava', 2, 'fire', null, 'Volcano Pokémon', 9, 190, 'Be careful if it turns its back during battle. It means that it will attack with the fire on its back.', 155, 'Level 14'),
  (157, 'Typhlosion', 2, 'fire', null, 'Volcano Pokémon', 17, 795, 'If its rage peaks, it becomes so hot that anything that touches it will instantly go up in flames.', 156, 'Level 36'),
  (158, 'Totodile', 2, 'water', null, 'Big Jaw Pokémon', 6, 95, 'Its powerful, well-developed jaws are capable of crushing anything. Even its Trainer must be careful.', null, null),
  (159, 'Croconaw', 2, 'water', null, 'Big Jaw Pokémon', 11, 250, 'If it loses a fang, a new one grows back in its place. There are always 48 fangs lining its mouth.', 158, 'Level 18'),
  (160, 'Feraligatr', 2, 'water', null, 'Big Jaw Pokémon', 23, 888, 'When it bites with its massive and powerful jaws, it shakes its head and savagely tears its victim up.', 159, 'Level 30'),
  (161, 'Sentret', 2, 'normal', null, 'Scout Pokémon', 8, 60, 'A very cautious Pokémon, it raises itself up using its tail to get a better view of its surroundings.', null, null),
  (162, 'Furret', 2, 'normal', null, 'Long Body Pokémon', 18, 325, 'It makes a nest to suit its long and skinny body. The nest is impossible for other Pokémon to enter.', 161, 'Level 15'),
  (163, 'Hoothoot', 2, 'normal', 'flying', 'Owl Pokémon', 7, 212, 'It always stands on one foot. It changes feet so fast, the movement can rarely be seen.', null, null),
  (164, 'Noctowl', 2, 'normal', 'flying', 'Owl Pokémon', 16, 408, 'Its eyes are specially adapted. They concentrate even faint light and enable it to see in the dark.', 163, 'Level 20'),
  (165, 'Ledyba', 2, 'bug', 'flying', 'Five Star Pokémon', 10, 108, 'It is very timid. It will be afraid to move if it is alone. But it will be active if it is in a group.', null, null),
  (166, 'Ledian', 2, 'bug', 'flying', 'Five Star Pokémon', 14, 356, 'When the stars flicker in the night sky, it flutters about, scattering a glowing powder.', 165, 'Level 18'),
  (167, 'Spinarak', 2, 'bug', 'poison', 'String Spit Pokémon', 5, 85, 'It lies still in the same pose for days in its web, waiting for its unsuspecting prey to wander close.', null, null),
  (168, 'Ariados', 2, 'bug', 'poison', 'Long Leg Pokémon', 11, 335, 'It spins string not only from its rear but also from its mouth. It’s hard to tell which end is which.', 167, 'Level 22'),
  (169, 'Crobat', 2, 'poison', 'flying', 'Bat Pokémon', 18, 750, 'It flies so silently through the dark on its four wings that it may not be noticed even when nearby.', 42, 'Friendship'),
  (170, 'Chinchou', 2, 'water', 'electric', 'Angler Pokémon', 5, 120, 'It shoots positive and negative electricity between the tips of its two antennae and zaps its enemies.', null, null),
  (171, 'Lanturn', 2, 'water', 'electric', 'Light Pokémon', 12, 225, 'The light it emits is so bright that it can illuminate the sea’s surface from a depth of over three miles.', 170, 'Level 27'),
  (172, 'Pichu', 2, 'electric', null, 'Tiny Mouse Pokémon', 3, 20, 'It is not yet skilled at storing electricity. It may send out a jolt if amused or startled.', null, null),
  (173, 'Cleffa', 2, 'fairy', null, 'Star Shape Pokémon', 3, 30, 'Because of its unusual, starlike silhouette, people believe that it came here on a meteor.', null, null),
  (174, 'Igglybuff', 2, 'normal', 'fairy', 'Balloon Pokémon', 3, 10, 'It has a very soft body. If it starts to roll, it will bounce all over and be impossible to stop.', null, null),
  (175, 'Togepi', 2, 'fairy', null, 'Spike Ball Pokémon', 3, 15, 'The shell seems to be filled with joy. It is said that it will share good luck when treated kindly.', null, null),
  (176, 'Togetic', 2, 'fairy', 'flying', 'Happiness Pokémon', 6, 32, 'They say that it will appear before kindhearted, caring people and shower them with happiness.', 175, 'Friendship'),
  (177, 'Natu', 2, 'psychic', 'flying', 'Tiny Bird Pokémon', 2, 20, 'Because its wings aren’t yet fully grown, it has to hop to get around. It is always staring at something.', null, null),
  (178, 'Xatu', 2, 'psychic', 'flying', 'Mystic Pokémon', 15, 150, 'They say that it stays still and quiet because it is seeing both the past and future at the same time.', 177, 'Level 25'),
  (179, 'Mareep', 2, 'electric', null, 'Wool Pokémon', 6, 78, 'If static electricity builds in its body, its fleece doubles in volume. Touching it will shock you.', null, null),
  (180, 'Flaaffy', 2, 'electric', null, 'Wool Pokémon', 8, 133, 'As a result of storing too much electricity, it developed patches where even downy wool won’t grow.', 179, 'Level 15'),
  (181, 'Ampharos', 2, 'electric', null, 'Light Pokémon', 14, 615, 'The tail’s tip shines brightly and can be seen from far away. It acts as a beacon for lost people.', 180, 'Level 30'),
  (182, 'Bellossom', 2, 'grass', null, 'Flower Pokémon', 4, 58, 'Bellossom gather at times and seem to dance. They say that the dance is a ritual to summon the sun.', 44, 'Sun Stone'),
  (183, 'Marill', 2, 'water', 'fairy', 'Aqua Mouse Pokémon', 4, 85, 'The tip of its tail, which contains oil that is lighter than water, lets it swim without drowning.', null, null),
  (184, 'Azumarill', 2, 'water', 'fairy', 'Aqua Rabbit Pokémon', 8, 285, 'By keeping still and listening intently, it can tell what is in even wild, fast-moving rivers.', 183, 'Level 18'),
  (185, 'Sudowoodo', 2, 'rock', null, 'Imitation Pokémon', 12, 380, 'Although it always pretends to be a tree, its composition appears more similar to rock than to vegetation.', null, null),
  (186, 'Politoed', 2, 'water', null, 'Frog Pokémon', 11, 339, 'If Poliwag and Poliwhirl hear its echoing cry, they respond by gathering from far and wide.', 61, 'Trade holding King''s Rock'),
  (187, 'Hoppip', 2, 'grass', 'flying', 'Cottonweed Pokémon', 4, 5, 'To keep from being blown away by the wind, they gather in clusters. But they do enjoy gentle breezes.', null, null),
  (188, 'Skiploom', 2, 'grass', 'flying', 'Cottonweed Pokémon', 6, 10, 'The bloom on top of its head opens and closes as the temperature fluctuates up and down.', 187, 'Level 18'),
  (189, 'Jumpluff', 2, 'grass', 'flying', 'Cottonweed Pokémon', 8, 30, 'Once it catches the wind, it deftly controls its cotton-puff spores-- it can even float around the world.', 188, 'Level 27'),
  (190, 'Aipom', 2, 'normal', null, 'Long Tail Pokémon', 8, 115, 'Its tail is so powerful that it can use it to grab a tree branch and hold itself up in the air.', null, null),
  (191, 'Sunkern', 2, 'grass', null, 'Seed Pokémon', 3, 18, 'It may plummet from the sky. If attacked by a Spearow, it will violently shake its leaves.', null, null),
  (192, 'Sunflora', 2, 'grass', null, 'Sun Pokémon', 8, 85, 'It converts sunlight into energy. In the darkness after sunset, it closes its petals and becomes still.', 191, 'Sun Stone'),
  (193, 'Yanma', 2, 'bug', 'flying', 'Clear Wing Pokémon', 12, 380, 'If it flaps its wings really fast, it can generate shock waves that will shatter windows in the area.', null, null),
  (194, 'Wooper', 2, 'water', 'ground', 'Water Fish Pokémon', 4, 85, 'This Pokémon lives in cold water. It will leave the water to search for food when it gets cold outside.', null, null),
  (195, 'Quagsire', 2, 'water', 'ground', 'Water Fish Pokémon', 14, 750, 'This carefree Pokémon has an easy-going nature. While swimming, it always bumps into boat hulls.', 194, 'Level 20'),
  (196, 'Espeon', 2, 'psychic', null, 'Sun Pokémon', 9, 265, 'It uses the fine hair that covers its body to sense air currents and predict its enemy’s actions.', 133, 'Friendship (day)'),
  (197, 'Umbreon', 2, 'dark', null, 'Moonlight Pokémon', 10, 270, 'When agitated, this Pokémon protects itself by spraying poisonous sweat from its pores.', 133, 'Friendship (night)'),
  (198, 'Murkrow', 2, 'dark', 'flying', 'Darkness Pokémon', 5, 21, 'Feared and loathed by many, it is believed to bring misfortune to all those who see it at night.', null, null),
  (199, 'Slowking', 2, 'water', 'psychic', 'Royal Pokémon', 20, 795, 'It has incredible intellect and intuition. Whatever the situation, it remains calm and collected.', 79, 'Trade holding King''s Rock'),
  (200, 'Misdreavus', 2, 'ghost', null, 'Screech Pokémon', 7, 10, 'It likes playing mischievous tricks, such as screaming and wailing to startle people at night.', null, null),
  (201, 'Unown', 2, 'psychic', null, 'Symbol Pokémon', 5, 50, 'Their shapes look like hieroglyphs on ancient tablets. It is said that the two are somehow related.', null, null),
  (202, 'Wobbuffet', 2, 'psychic', null, 'Patient Pokémon', 13, 285, 'It hates light and shock. If attacked, it inflates its body to build up its counterstrike.', null, null),
  (203, 'Girafarig', 2, 'normal', 'psychic', 'Long Neck Pokémon', 15, 415, 'Its tail has a small brain of its own. Beware! If you get close, it may react to your scent by biting.', null, null),
  (204, 'Pineco', 2, 'bug', null, 'Bagworm Pokémon', 6, 72, 'It likes to make its shell thicker by adding layers of tree bark. The additional weight doesn’t bother it.', null, null),
  (205, 'Forretress', 2, 'bug', 'steel', 'Bagworm Pokémon', 12, 1258, 'Its entire body is shielded by a steel-hard shell. What lurks inside this shell is a total mystery.', 204, 'Level 31'),
  (206, 'Dunsparce', 2, 'normal', null, 'Land Snake Pokémon', 15, 140, 'When spotted, this Pokémon escapes backward by furiously boring into the ground with its tail.', null, null),
  (207, 'Gligar', 2, 'ground', 'flying', 'Fly Scorpion Pokémon', 11, 648, 'It flies straight at its target’s face, then clamps down on the startled victim to inject poison.', null, null),
  (208, 'Steelix', 2, 'steel', 'ground', 'Iron Snake Pokémon', 92, 4000, 'Its body has been compressed deep under the ground. As a result, it is even harder than a diamond.', 95, 'Trade holding Metal Coat'),
  (209, 'Snubbull', 2, 'fairy', null, 'Fairy Pokémon', 6, 78, 'Although it looks frightening, it is actually kind and affectionate. It is very popular among women.', null, null),
  (210, 'Granbull', 2, 'fairy', null, 'Fairy Pokémon', 14, 487, 'It is actually timid and easily spooked. If attacked, it flails about to fend off its attacker.', 209, 'Level 23'),
  (211, 'Qwilfish', 2, 'water', 'poison', 'Balloon Pokémon', 5, 39, 'To fire its poison spikes, it must inflate its body by drinking over 2.6 gallons of water all at once.', null, null),
  (212, 'Scizor', 2, 'bug', 'steel', 'Pincer Pokémon', 18, 1180, 'It swings its eye-patterned pincers up to scare its foes. This makes it look like it has three heads.', 123, 'Trade holding Metal Coat'),
  (213, 'Shuckle', 2, 'bug', 'rock', 'Mold Pokémon', 6, 205, 'The berries it stores in its vase-like shell decompose and become a gooey liquid.', null, null),
  (214, 'Heracross', 2, 'bug', 'fighting', 'Single Horn Pokémon', 15, 540, 'This powerful Pokémon thrusts its prized horn under its enemies’ bellies, then lifts and throws them.', null, null),
  (215, 'Sneasel', 2, 'dark', 'ice', 'Sharp Claw Pokémon', 9, 280, 'Its paws conceal sharp claws. If attacked, it suddenly extends the claws and startles its enemy.', null, null),
  (216, 'Teddiursa', 2, 'normal', null, 'Little Bear Pokémon', 6, 88, 'If it finds honey, its crescent mark glows. It always licks its paws because they’re soaked with honey.', null, null),
  (217, 'Ursaring', 2, 'normal', null, 'Hibernator Pokémon', 18, 1258, 'Although it is a good climber, it prefers to snap trees with its forelegs and eat fallen berries.', 216, 'Level 30'),
  (218, 'Slugma', 2, 'fire', null, 'Lava Pokémon', 7, 350, 'It never sleeps. It has to keep moving because if it stopped, its magma body would cool and harden.', null, null),
  (219, 'Magcargo', 2, 'fire', 'rock', 'Lava Pokémon', 8, 550, 'The shell on its back is just skin that has cooled and hardened. It breaks easily with a slight touch.', 218, 'Level 38'),
  (220, 'Swinub', 2, 'ice', 'ground', 'Pig Pokémon', 4, 65, 'It rubs its snout on the ground to find and dig up food. It sometimes discovers hot springs.', null, null),
  (221, 'Piloswine', 2, 'ice', 'ground', 'Swine Pokémon', 11, 558, 'Because the long hair all over its body obscures its sight, it just keeps charging repeatedly.', 220, 'Level 33'),
  (222, 'Corsola', 2, 'water', 'rock', 'Coral Pokémon', 6, 50, 'It continuously sheds and grows. The tip of its head is prized as a treasure because of its beauty.', null, null),
  (223, 'Remoraid', 2, 'water', null, 'Jet Pokémon', 6, 120, 'It has superb accuracy. The water it shoots out can strike moving prey from more than 300 feet away.', null, null),
  (224, 'Octillery', 2, 'water', null, 'Jet Pokémon', 9, 285, 'It traps foes with the suction cups on its tentacles, then smashes them with its rock-hard head.', 223, 'Level 25'),
  (225, 'Delibird', 2, 'ice', 'flying', 'Delivery Pokémon', 9, 160, 'It carries food all day long. There are tales about lost people who were saved by its stored food.', null, null),
  (226, 'Mantine', 2, 'water', 'flying', 'Kite Pokémon', 21, 2200, 'As it majestically swims, it doesn’t care if Remoraid attach to it for scavenging its leftovers.', null, null),
  (227, 'Skarmory', 2, 'steel', 'flying', 'Armor Bird Pokémon', 17, 505, 'Its sturdy wings look heavy, but they are actually hollow and light, allowing it to fly freely in the sky.', null, null),
  (228, 'Houndour', 2, 'dark', 'fire', 'Dark Pokémon', 6, 108, 'It uses different kinds of cries for communicating with others of its kind and for pursuing its prey.', null, null),
  (229, 'Houndoom', 2, 'dark', 'fire', 'Dark Pokémon', 14, 350, 'If you are burned by the flames it shoots from its mouth, the pain will never go away.', 228, 'Level 24'),
  (230, 'Kingdra', 2, 'water', 'dragon', 'Dragon Pokémon', 18, 1520, 'It is said that it usually hides in underwater caves. It can create whirlpools by yawning.', 117, 'Trade holding Dragon Scale'),
  (231, 'Phanpy', 2, 'ground', null, 'Long Nose Pokémon', 5, 335, 'It swings its long snout around playfully, but because it is so strong, that can be dangerous.', null, null),
  (232, 'Donphan', 2, 'ground', null, 'Armor Pokémon', 11, 1200, 'It has sharp, hard tusks and a rugged hide. Its tackle is strong enough to knock down a house.', 231, 'Level 25'),
  (233, 'Porygon2', 2, 'normal', null, 'Virtual Pokémon', 6, 325, 'This upgraded version of Porygon is designed for space exploration. It can’t fly, however.', 137, 'Trade holding Up-Grade'),
  (234, 'Stantler', 2, 'normal', null, 'Big Horn Pokémon', 14, 712, 'The curved antlers subtly change the flow of air to create a strange space where reality is distorted.', null, null),
  (235, 'Smeargle', 2, 'normal', null, 'Painter Pokémon', 12, 580, 'A special fluid oozes from the tip of its tail. It paints the fluid everywhere to mark its territory.', null, null),
  (236, 'Tyrogue', 2, 'fighting', null, 'Scuffle Pokémon', 7, 210, 'It is always bursting with energy. To make itself stronger, it keeps on fighting even if it loses.', null, null),
  (237, 'Hitmontop', 2, 'fighting', null, 'Handstand Pokémon', 14, 480, 'If you are enchanted by its smooth, dance-like kicks, you may get a closer experience with one than you’d like.', 236, 'Level 20, Attack = Defense'),
  (238, 'Smoochum', 2, 'ice', 'psychic', 'Kiss Pokémon', 4, 60, 'Its lips are the most sensitive part of its body. It always uses its lips first to examine things.', null, null),
  (239, 'Elekid', 2, 'electric', null, 'Electric Pokémon', 6, 235, 'It rotates its arms to generate electricity, but it tires easily, so it only charges up a little bit.', null, null),
  (240, 'Magby', 2, 'fire', null, 'Live Coal Pokémon', 7, 214, 'Each and every time it inhales and exhales, hot embers dribble from its mouth and nostrils.', null, null),
  (241, 'Miltank', 2, 'normal', null, 'Milk Cow Pokémon', 12, 755, 'Its milk is packed with nutrition, making it the ultimate beverage for the sick or weary.', null, null),
  (242, 'Blissey', 2, 'normal', null, 'Happiness Pokémon', 15, 468, 'Anyone who takes even one taste of Blissey’s egg becomes unfailingly caring and pleasant to everyone.', 113, 'Friendship'),
  (243, 'Raikou', 2, 'electric', null, 'Thunder Pokémon', 19, 1780, 'The rain clouds it carries let it fire thunderbolts at will. They say that it descended with lightning.', null, null),
  (244, 'Entei', 2, 'fire', null, 'Volcano Pokémon', 21, 1980, 'Volcanoes erupt when it barks. Unable to contain its sheer power, it races headlong around the land.', null, null),
  (245, 'Suicune', 2, 'water', null, 'Aurora Pokémon', 20, 1870, 'Said to be the embodiment of north winds, it can instantly purify filthy, murky water.', null, null),
  (246, 'Larvitar', 2, 'rock', 'ground', 'Rock Skin Pokémon', 6, 720, 'It feeds on soil. After it has eaten a large mountain, it falls asleep so it can grow.', null, null),
  (247, 'Pupitar', 2, 'rock', 'ground', 'Hard Shell Pokémon', 12, 1520, 'Its shell is as hard as sheet rock, and it is also very strong. Its thrashing can topple a mountain.', 246, 'Level 30'),
  (248, 'Tyranitar', 2, 'rock', 'dark', 'Armor Pokémon', 20, 2020, 'Its body can’t be harmed by any sort of attack, so it is very eager to make challenges against enemies.', 247, 'Level 55'),
  (249, 'Lugia', 2, 'psychic', 'flying', 'Diving Pokémon', 52, 2160, 'It is said that it quietly spends its time deep at the bottom of the sea because its powers are too strong.', null, null),
  (250, 'Ho-Oh', 2, 'fire', 'flying', 'Rainbow Pokémon', 38, 1990, 'Legends claim this Pokémon flies the world’s skies continuously on its magnificent, seven-colored wings.', null, null),
  (251, 'Celebi', 2, 'psychic', 'grass', 'Time Travel Pokémon', 6, 50, 'This Pokémon wanders across time. Grass and trees flourish in the forests in which it has appeared.', null, null);
